<title>CHINA: ASIASAT INTERIM NET RISES 85 4 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>ASIASAT INTERIM NET RISES 85 4 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   79.0	vs  43.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0	 vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  41.6 gain vs  19.5 loss</p>
<p>    Net			   309.5	vs 166.9</p>
<p>    Turnover		    507.7	vs 357.7</p>
<p>    Company name		Asia Satellite Telecommunications</p>
<p>				    Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 September 18-25</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  November 4</p>
<p>NOTE - Satellite operator Asia Satellite is owned in equal parts by Hutchison Whampoa Ltd, Britain's Cable &amp; Wireless Plc and Beijing's state-owned flagship China International Trust and Investment Corp (CITIC).</p>
<p>Comparative figures have been reclassified to conform with the current year's presentation.</p>
<p>The exceptional gain for the six months ended June 30, 1997 arose from the disposal of a 99 percent equity interest in the First Asian Satellite Leasing Ltd Partnership. The exceptional charge for the corresponding period ended June 30, 1996 and the year ended December 31, 1996 were the flotation expenses in connection with the initial public offering.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
